{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2629234","formula":"Cl₂O₃","hill":"Cl2O3","elements":["O","Cl"],"composition":{"O":3.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Dichlorine trioxide","ru":"Триоксид дихлора"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dichlorine trioxide, Cl2O3, is a chlorine oxide. It is a dark brown solid discovered in 1967 which is explosive even below 0 °C. It is formed by the low-temperature photolysis of ClO2 and is formed along with Cl2O6, Cl2 and O2. Its structure is believed to be OCl−ClO2 with possible isomers such as Cl−O−ClO2.","ru":"Триоксид дихлора — химическое соединение с формулой Cl2O3. Это тёмно-коричневое твёрдое вещество, открытое в 1967 году, взрывоопасно даже при температуре ниже 0 °C. Оно образуется в результате низкотемпературного фотолиза ClO2 и образуется вместе с Cl2O6, Cl2 и O2. Считается, что его структура представляет собой OCl−ClO2 с возможными изомерами, такими как Cl−O−ClO2."},"fame":20,"pubchemCid":167661,"mass":118.9,"charge":0,"smiles":"O=ClCl(=O)=O","inchikey":"XGNLKXPXDGCHRZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2629234","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dichlorine_trioxide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A2%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BE%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%B4_%D0%B4%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/167661","license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q422080","formula":"ClO₂","names":{"en":"Chlorine dioxide","ru":"Диоксид хлора"},"elements":["O","Cl"],"fame":40,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q593248","formula":"ClO₂⁻","names":{"en":"Chlorite",